From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morris <jmorris@namei.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] lib: sbi: read a commit record's flag once when
 printing it

sbi_dcommit_report() runs on the HART that resets the system, while
another HART may still be committing. It reads that HART's committed
flag twice: once for the first line of the record and once to decide
whether to print the rest. A commit between the two reads prints a
record that says the HART is not committed, followed by the PMP entries
of a committed HART. Nothing orders the flag after the readback either,
so a report that sees the flag set may print a readback that is not yet
complete.

Read the flag once into a local, with a read barrier after it, and use
the local for both. In sbi_dcommit_seal_hart(), put a write barrier
before the flag is set, so that a report that sees the flag set also
sees the readback, menvcfg and mseccfg of that HART. A record is then
printed whole, as not committed or as committed.

AI-assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), in the GitHub Copilot CLI
---
 docs/domain_support.md |  5 ++++-
 lib/sbi/sbi_dcommit.c  | 14 ++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/domain_support.md b/docs/domain_support.md
index 01d16ce..112389a 100644
--- a/docs/domain_support.md
+++ b/docs/domain_support.md
@@ -157,7 +157,10 @@ back to it, how many SBI calls its allowlist refused, how many allowed
 calls returned an error, and, once committed, its **menvcfg**, **mseccfg**
 and first 16 PMP entries. When the device tree holds a configuration
 digest, OpenSBI prints the digest at boot and every record just before a
-system reset.
+system reset. A HART that commits while the records are printed has its
+record printed whole, as not committed or as committed: it sets its
+committed flag only after the rest of its record, and the report reads
+the flag once, before the rest.
 
 The per-HART contexts of domain switches are allocated once at boot, for
 every HART in every domain that lists it, so a switch never allocates.
diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_dcommit.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_dcommit.c
index 161993d..df4348b 100644
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_dcommit.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_dcommit.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <sbi/riscv_asm.h>
+#include <sbi/riscv_barrier.h>
 #include <sbi/riscv_encoding.h>
 #include <sbi/sbi_console.h>
 #include <sbi/sbi_dcommit.h>
@@ -103,6 +104,8 @@ int sbi_dcommit_seal_hart(struct sbi_scratch *scratch, struct sbi_domain *dom)
 	rec->menvcfg = has_menvcfg ? csr_read64(CSR_MENVCFG) : 0;
 	rec->mseccfg = sbi_hart_has_extension(scratch, SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP) ?
 		       csr_read64(CSR_MSECCFG) : 0;
+	/* The record before its flag, for sbi_dcommit_report() */
+	smp_wmb();
 	rec->committed = 1;
 
 	return 0;
@@ -181,6 +184,7 @@ void sbi_dcommit_report(void)
 {
 	const struct sbi_dcommit_hart *rec;
 	u32 i, j, hartid;
+	u64 committed;
 
 	if (!dcommit_digest_set)
 		return;
@@ -188,13 +192,19 @@ void sbi_dcommit_report(void)
 	for (i = 0; i < sbi_hart_count(); i++) {
 		rec = &sbi_dcommit_harts[i];
 		hartid = sbi_hartindex_to_hartid(i);
+		/*
+		 * The HART may commit while this one prints: read its flag
+		 * once, and the rest of its record only after the flag.
+		 */
+		committed = rec->committed;
+		smp_rmb();
 		sbi_printf("Domain commit hart%u: committed=%llu pmp_faults=%llu "
 			   "blocked_calls=%llu failed_calls=%llu\n", hartid,
-			   (unsigned long long)rec->committed,
+			   (unsigned long long)committed,
 			   (unsigned long long)rec->pmp_faults,
 			   (unsigned long long)rec->blocked_calls,
 			   (unsigned long long)rec->failed_calls);
-		if (!rec->committed)
+		if (!committed)
 			continue;
 
 		sbi_printf("Domain commit hart%u: menvcfg=0x%016llx "
